1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Your phone is already an always-on computer. Why rent a server to run an agent?

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:09,000
phone-agent runs a Pi coding agent entirely inside a Chrome tab on an Android phone:
agent loop, bash, filesystem, Python. Nothing installed on the phone.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:12,500
Launching from scratch: joins the tailnet, restores files + transcript, attests the Tinfoil enclave. ~2 s.

4
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:18,000
The tab is a real Tailscale node. The chat page on the left is served by the phone to the laptop. No relay.

5
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:26,000
"What did we do earlier?" It remembers: the transcript lives in browser storage and survives restarts.

6
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:34,000
Replies come from DeepSeek on Tinfoil through an attested, encrypted channel verified by the phone.

7
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:40,000
"Show your golfed Fibonacci code and run it again."

8
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:47,000
The python tool: CPython in WebAssembly, in a sandboxed worker, sharing the agent's files. Loaded in 2 s.

9
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Output streams back over server-sent events. The phone did all of it.

10
00:00:52,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Pi + Tailscale + Pyodide, in one tab, on a phone, controlled from anywhere on the tailnet. phone-agent.
